cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite the paper (preferred citation) and this repository."
type: software
title: "Code and data for: Heritable variance in fitness in wild vertebrates accounts for a small share of their missing neutral diversity and exceeds what recurrent mutation is estimated to maintain"
authors:
  - family-names: Mawass
    given-names: Walid
    affiliation: "Department of Human Genetics, University of Chicago"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-24
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/mawassw/va-fitness-diversity"
abstract: >-
  R scripts and curated data that take the additive genetic variance in relative fitness
  estimated by Bonnet et al. (2022) in 19 wild vertebrate pedigrees through two equilibrium
  tests: how much neutral diversity that variance removes, relative to the diversity each
  population is missing, and how much of it recurrent deleterious mutation can maintain at
  mutation-selection-drift balance. The scripts reproduce every figure and table of the paper.
keywords:
  - additive genetic variance in fitness
  - effective population size
  - neutral diversity
  - mutation-selection-drift balance
  - linked selection
  - wild vertebrate pedigrees
